 - `?assignee=<user id>` or `?assignee=none`: only the tasks assigned to this user, or to nobody;
 - `?sort=`: `position` (the default, ascending), `due_date` (soonest first, tasks without one last), `priority`
   (highest first) or `created` (newest first). Ties go by id: ascending, except for `created` where the newest
   comes first.
 
+Tasks come in pages, in the order of the sort: `?limit=` is the size of a page (1 to 200, default 50; anything else
+answers 400), and `?cursor=` asks for the page after another one. `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page; otherwise
+pass it back as `cursor`, with the same filters and sort, to get the next page. A cursor is an opaque string that
+only works with the list and the sort it came from: any other `cursor` answers 400. Pages are cut on the sort key,
+not on a count, so a task added or removed between two requests does not make another one come twice or be skipped.
+
+```
+GET /api/lists/3/tasks?sort=due_date&limit=2
+→ { "items": [<task>, <task>], "next_cursor": "eyJs…" }
+GET /api/lists/3/tasks?sort=due_date&limit=2&cursor=eyJs…
+→ { "items": [<task>], "next_cursor": null }
+```
